Migrations land here in Phase 1, forward-only and numbered:

  0001_extensions.sql       uuid-ossp, btree_gist, pgcrypto, citext
  0002_plans.sql            subscription_plans + seeded tiers
  0003_tenancy.sql          businesses, business_members, branches, platform_admins
  0004_catalog.sql          services, staff_resources, staff_services
  0005_availability.sql     availability_rules, availability_overrides
  0006_crm.sql              customers
  0007_bookings.sql         bookings (+ blocked_range GIST), booking_history
  0008_waitlist.sql         waitlist_entries
  0009_notifications.sql    notification_templates, notification_logs
  0010_payments.sql         payments, subscription_invoices, sms_topups
  0011_indexes.sql          performance indexes
  0012_triggers.sql         updated_at triggers, booking-code sequence

Create one with `npx supabase migration new <name>` so the timestamp prefix is
consistent. Never edit a migration that has been applied to staging or
production — write a new one.

Apply the corrections in docs/DEVELOPMENT_PLAN.md §13 as you port the spec's
SQL. In particular the bookings table must exclude on a buffer-inclusive
`blocked_range`, not on `slot_range` (defect B-03), or the database will permit
buffer violations that the slot picker believes it prevented.
